1
00:05:15,789 --> 00:05:21,789
You're never too small to dream big.

2
00:10:31,578 --> 00:10:37,578
GOAT is a animation, comedy, family film directed by Tyree Dillihay.

3
00:15:47,368 --> 00:15:53,368
Will, a small goat with big dreams, gets a once-in-a-lifetime shot to join the pros and play roarball – a
high-intensity, co-ed, full-contact sport dominated by the fastest, fiercest animals in the world.

4
00:21:03,157 --> 00:21:09,157
Will's new teammates aren't thrilled about having a little goat on their roster, but Will is
determined to revolutionize the sport and prove once and for all that 'smalls can ball'!

5
00:26:18,947 --> 00:26:24,947
He has to do something he has never done before.

6
00:31:34,736 --> 00:31:40,736
Will Harris (voice), played by Caleb McLaughlin.

7
00:36:50,526 --> 00:36:56,526
Jett Fillmore  (voice), played by Gabrielle Union.

8
00:42:06,315 --> 00:42:12,315
Florence Everson  (voice), played by Jenifer Lewis.

9
00:47:22,105 --> 00:47:28,105
Archie Everhardt  (voice), played by David Harbour.

10
00:52:37,894 --> 00:52:43,894
Modo Olachenko  (voice), played by Nick Kroll.

11
00:57:53,684 --> 00:57:59,684
Olivia Burke  (voice), played by Nicola Coughlan.

12
01:03:09,473 --> 01:03:15,473
Goat is an upcoming American animated sports comedy film directed by Tyree Dillihay from a screenplay
by Aaron Buchsbaum and Teddy Riley and story by Nicolas Curcio and Peter Chiarelli.

13
01:08:25,263 --> 01:08:31,263
The film stars Caleb McLaughlin, alongside an ensemble voice cast including Gabrielle Union, Stephen Curry (who is also producer on the film), Nicola Coughlan, Nick
Kroll, David Harbour, Jenifer Lewis, Aaron Pierre, Patton Oswalt, Andrew Santino, Bobby Lee, Eduardo Franco, Sherry Cola, Jelly Roll and Jennifer Hudson.

14
01:13:41,052 --> 01:13:47,052
It follows an anthropomorphic goat named Will Harris who aspires to become the
greatest of all time at a basketball-like sport known as roarball.

15
01:18:56,842 --> 01:19:02,842
The film was being developed by 2019 and announced in May 2024,
with most of the cast being announced in June 2025.

16
01:24:12,631 --> 01:24:18,631
It is scheduled to be released in the United States on
February 13, 2026, by Sony Pictures Releasing.

17
01:29:28,421 --> 01:29:34,421
The film explores themes of underdog, friendship,
bullying, challenge, basketball.

18
01:34:44,210 --> 01:34:50,210
The tone is lighthearted and uplifting.
